{"id": "EUVD-2026-63800", "enisaUuid": "058a62a4-885c-3c71-8aaf-d5472be6129a", "description": "A flaw was found in the clusterclaims-controller component of multicluster engine (MCE). A tenant with standard permissions to create and delete ClusterClaim resources can exploit this by manipulating the `spec.namespace` field. This allows the tenant to specify and delete any ManagedCluster, including the hub's local-cluster or other tenants' clusters, due to a missing ownership check. This vulnerability can lead to a denial of service by enabling unauthorized deletion of ManagedClusters.", "datePublished": "2026-08-21T02:43:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-29T19:41:34", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59556", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59557", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59558", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59559", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59579", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:59593", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-73267", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2514218"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q3cg-8r2r-6g4g", "CVE-2026-73267"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.63, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3b73a5f4-1c0a-3acf-9ca9-e79b8fa6093f", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.17", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1786577950"}, {"id": "698c0797-c1ee-3695-a322-7713151bf187", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1787259059"}, {"id": "86fefe10-83c9-3d42-b016-820b77b9a988", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1787195995"}, {"id": "aa4ade3e-fa01-3e60-957d-3864661c57f8", "product": {"name": "multicluster engine for Kubernetes 2.6", "vendor": {"n